From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 11:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 312/312] avutil/hwcontext_v4l2request: define the AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
 fourccs when missing

The AFBC capture formats added for Cedrus are guarded by
#if defined(V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_{8,10}_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT). Distribution
linux/videodev2.h (e.g. Ubuntu linux-libc-dev) does not carry these
definitions yet, so a packaged build silently drops the AFBC path and
Cedrus 10-bit output (VP9/HEVC/AVS2 Main10) cannot be imported.

Provide the kernel uAPI fourccs ('AS12', 'AS01') as #ifndef fallbacks,
like the local v4l2-stateless-*.h headers do for the controls. They step
aside once the kernel headers define them.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index b6633d9081..6705cee48d 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -34,6 +34,18 @@
 #include "hwcontext_v4l2request_internal.h"
 #include "mem.h"
 
+/*
+ * Cedrus AFBC capture formats (Jernej Skrabec's sunxi media patches, not yet in
+ * linux/videodev2.h of most distributions). The fourccs are fixed by the kernel
+ * uAPI; the driver only enumerates them when it supports them.
+ */
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_8_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_8_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT  v4l2_fourcc('A', 'S', '1', '2')
+#endif
+#ifndef V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT
+#define V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420_10_AFBC_16X16_SPLIT v4l2_fourcc('A', 'S', '0', '1')
+#endif
+
 typedef struct V4L2RequestVideoDecoder {
     dev_t media_dev;
     dev_t video_dev;
